## 5) Canonical Wire Contract

The modern runtime contract is:

- events: `POST {STACKTRACE_ENDPOINT}/v1/events`
- spans: `POST {STACKTRACE_ENDPOINT}/v1/spans`

Event body:

```json
{ "events": [] }
```

Batch rule:

- `events` must be an array with `1..100` event objects
- the batch object must not include extra top-level keys

Span body:

```json
{ "spans": [] }
```

Batch rule:

- `spans` must be an array with `1..500` span objects
- the batch object must not include extra top-level keys

Do not use legacy runtime paths in new clients:

- `/ingest/error`
- `/ingest/log`

Events must be canonical v4 after SDK normalization:

- each item has `schema_version: 4` (do not send the legacy `schemaVersion`)
- each item has `type` ∈ `log | error` — the v3 `performance` type was removed; request/operation timing lives in spans, not in a log event
- W3C-hex trace ids: `trace_id` is 32 lowercase hex, `span_id`/`parent_span_id` are 16 lowercase hex, so events reconcile with the `traceparent` header and with span rows
- snake_case throughout; unsupported extra top-level fields are rejected (strict)

Source of truth: `packages/shared/schema/canonical-event-v4.schema.ts` (`EventSchemaV4`); contract doc `docs/contracts/payload-v4.md`. Legacy v1/v2/v3 payloads are rejected at the ingest boundary with HTTP 400.

Accepted v4 event fields:

| Field            | Type                                                         | Required        | Notes                                               |
| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| `schema_version` | literal `4`                                                  | yes             | do not send `schemaVersion`                         |
| `tenant_id`      | UUID string                                                  | no              | server-owned; ingestion fills from API key          |
| `project_id`     | UUID string                                                  | no              | server-owned; ingestion fills from API key          |
| `event_id`       | UUID string                                                  | yes             | generated by SDK (idempotency key)                  |
| `timestamp`      | ISO timestamp string                                         | yes             | client event timestamp                              |
| `type`           | `log` \| `error`                                             | yes             | no `performance`; request timing lives in spans     |
| `level`          | `trace` \| `debug` \| `info` \| `warn` \| `error` \| `fatal` | yes             | match event severity                                |
| `message`        | string `1..64000`                                            | yes             | sanitized, bounded                                  |
| `service_id`     | UUID string                                                  | yes             | copied from `STACKTRACE_SERVICE_ID`                 |
| `service`        | object                                                       | yes             | see service fields below (`name`/`version`/`environment`) |
| `trace`          | object                                                       | yes             | see trace fields below; `span_id` required; W3C-hex ids |
| `metadata`       | object                                                       | yes             | structured (`http`, `db`, `business`, `correlation`, `tags`, …); use `{}` when empty |
| `error`          | object                                                       | only for errors | see error fields below                              |

