## 12) Security and Privacy

Never emit:

- passwords
- access tokens
- API keys
- cookies
- authorization headers
- raw payment/card data
- connection strings
- full CPF/SSN/national IDs
- full request/response bodies unless explicitly approved

Always:

- redact headers before telemetry
- sanitize nested metadata
- mask sensitive identifiers
- limit string sizes
- avoid full model snapshots
- avoid full ORM payloads
- avoid logging SQL with interpolated user input

Headers such as `x-api-key`, `authorization`, `cookie`, and `set-cookie` must never be sent in telemetry.

